<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">What this guide is for</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    A pilot is a small, time-limited test of one agent on one workflow, designed to produce a decision. This guide gives a four-week plan, the measures to track and a checklist. It is written for owners and managers, and it suits a business that has chosen a candidate task but not yet committed.
  </p>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    The plan is our own. It is built on public guidance: Anthropic advises finding “the simplest solution possible, and only increasing complexity when needed”, and Microsoft advises using “the lowest level of complexity that reliably meets your requirements”. Where we state a step as a recommendation, we say it is ours. For background on what agents are, read our <a href="/resources/ai-agents-small-business-playbook-ebook/" class="font-medium text-[#5a9100] hover:underline">plain-English playbook</a>.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Before day 1: five decisions</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Our own suggestion, not a finding from the sources: settle these before anyone builds anything.
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    <li><strong>One workflow.</strong> Repeated often, easy to define as done, cheap to get wrong and quick to check. Answering customer questions from your own documents and booking appointments are two examples from our published guidance.</li>
    <li><strong>One owner.</strong> A named person who answers for the result, as for a member of staff.</li>
    <li><strong>One baseline.</strong> Record today’s numbers for the workflow: volume, time per item, error rate, cost including staff time. Without these, any before and after is guesswork.</li>
    <li><strong>One access list.</strong> Write down exactly what the agent may read and change. Start with read-only.</li>
    <li><strong>One stop rule.</strong> Decide in advance what would make you pause the pilot, such as a wrong message sent to a customer or access beyond the list.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">The plan at a glance</h2>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-left"><thead><tr><th class="border-b border-gray-200 py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7280]">Week</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7280]">Goal</th><th class="border-b border-gray-200 py-3 pr-4 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#6B7280]">Output</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">1</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Define and measure</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Written scope, access list, baseline numbers, success thresholds</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">2</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Build and test privately</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Working agent tested on past cases, with logging switched on</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">3</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Run alongside people</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Agent drafts, a person approves every result</td></tr><tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">4</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Limited live run and decision</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-3 pr-4 align-top text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">Results against baseline and a continue, adjust or stop decision</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
